## ADAPTATION GUIDELINES FOR AI SYSTEM

**When generating a policy, the AI should:**

1. **Collect Context First:**
   - Organization type, size, sector
   - Geographic location (affects regulations)
   - Technical maturity
   - Existing controls
   - Specific policy type needed

2. **Select Relevant Regulations:**
   - Based on geography (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)
   - Based on sector (HIPAA, PCI DSS, etc.)
   - Based on organization type (NIS2, critical infrastructure)

3. **Scale Complexity:**
   - Small org (< 50 people): Simpler processes, combined roles, less formal
   - Medium org (50-500): Defined roles, structured processes
   - Large org (500+): Detailed procedures, multiple approval layers, formal governance

4. **Include Practical Elements:**
   - Timeline/SLAs appropriate to org size
   - Forms and templates ready to use
   - Clear ownership assignments
   - Realistic review frequencies

5. **Ensure Completeness:**
   - All 11 core sections present
   - Appropriate appendices
   - Document control
   - Citations to sources

6. **Maintain Consistency:**
   - Terminology consistent throughout
   - Cross-references accurate
   - Role names match across sections

7. **Cite Sources:**
   - Reference specific regulations, articles, controls
   - Cite frameworks and standards used
   - Note where best practices applied

